      "rev_n_3_bf2f1d_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_bf2f1d_0",
        "node_id": "n_3_bf2f1d",
        "thought_text": "Find the centroid of the boat shape to use as a starting point for bulkhead placement.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "root",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794534663.988025
      },
      "rev_n_1_1a269d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_1a269d_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_1a269d",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous reasoning was in the calculation of the bulkhead placements. The ratio should be (i / (M - 1)) instead of (i / M), and the x_placement calculation should use this ratio correctly. Additionally, the placements need to be sorted in increasing order of X-coordinate. These changes should resolve the issue and produce the correct output.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_1a269d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_196d3afbf0",
        "created_at": 1794534692.2528422
      },
      "rev_n_2_e31d19_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_e31d19_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_e31d19",
        "thought_text": "The error in the output is due to the calculation of bulkhead placements. The current implementation uses integer division to determine the number of bulkheads, which can lead to rounding errors. To improve accuracy, we should use floating-point division and round the results to the nearest integer for the number of bulkheads. This will ensure that we have the correct number of placements and their positions are more precise.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_e31d19_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_e48ac5ff1a",
        "created_at": 1794534727.6621358
      },
      "rev_n_3_bf2f1d_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_bf2f1d_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_bf2f1d",
        "thought_text": "The error in the previous solution was due to using the centroid as a starting point for bulkhead placement, which doesn't account for the shape of the boat. Instead, we should use the length of the boat's longest side as a reference for placement. This approach will ensure that bulkheads are placed equidistant along the length of the ship, regardless of its shape.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_3_bf2f1d_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_b4d9c0e775",
        "created_at": 1794534762.5149736
      },
      "rev_n_4_0f7a30_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_4_0f7a30_0",
        "node_id": "n_4_0f7a30",
        "thought_text": "Review the loop for calculating placements. Ensure it iterates M-1 times and uses the correct ratio (i / (M - 1)) for placement calculation.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "-7508701118012346505",
        "replaces_revision_id": null,
        "feedback_id": null,
        "created_at": 1794534790.053137
      },
      "rev_n_5_d09b58_0": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_5_d09b58_0",
        "node_id": "n_5_d09b58",
        "thought_text": "Check the x_placement calculation. It should use the ratio to find the correct x-coordinate for each placement, ensuring it's within the bounds of the polygon.",
